  "body": "## What changed\n\nCarry a flipped X, Y, or XY WCS with a Z rotation in Bake and Control modes.\nReverse the G68 or ROT angle when exactly one XY axis is flipped.\nKeep the angle when both axes are flipped.\nAllow the supported frame through the app verification gate.\nKeep named refusals for tilted frames and other unsupported cases.\nUpdate the MCP capability description.\nRecord the composition decision in `docs/decisions/2476-flip-rotation.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe app and post refused every WCS that combined a flip with a rotation.\nA reflection changes the angle sign of a rotation in its frame.\nThe existing flip-before-rotate order works when the flip pass also changes that angle.\n\n## Tests\n\nThese pins failed on unchanged upstream code with the combined-frame refusal:\n\n- `flipped_yaw_bake_traces_the_cam_path`\n- `flipped_yaw_control_traces_the_cam_path_in_each_rotation_dialect`\n- `flipped_yaw_posts_in_bake_and_control_and_preserves_the_viewer_path`\n- `flipped_yaw_travel_checks_the_mirrored_table_path_in_both_modes`\n\nAll four pass with the fix.\nThe controller reader calibration passes before and after the fix.\nThe post pins trace X, Y, and XY flips at 30, -37, and 90 degrees.\nThey cover Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM, and Sinumerik in both modes.\nThe fixture includes arcs, a helix, compensation, a drilled hole, and a nonzero origin.\nThe app pins check viewer coordinates, setup sheets, travel limits, and off-Z refusal.\n\nRestoring the old post flip module makes the Bake pin fail.\nRestoring the fix makes it pass.\nDisabling the angle correction makes the Control pin fail.\nRestoring the correction makes it pass.\nRestoring the old app validation makes the app posting pin fail.\nRestoring the fix makes it pass.\nRestoring the old engine order still passes because the corrected angle makes it equivalent.\nThe final patch keeps that original order and removes the unnecessary reorder.\n\nThe quick gate passes all 79 steps.\nClippy passes both touched crates with `--all-targets -- -D warnings`.\nThe existing WCS flip suites pass: 15 post tests and 10 app tests.\nThe self-review accounts for every code and test hunk.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe `.nc` and `.cl` diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical controller or machine ran the programs.\nThe release gate did not run.\nFlipped Z, probing, off-Z tilt, and Control with inverted machine axes remain refused.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2714 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes `op_problem` in `crates/app/src/setup_wcs_flip.rs`.\nThis PR changes `setup_problem`.\n\nEffort: max\n\nChangelog: Post a flipped XY WCS with a Z rotation in Bake and Control modes, with the controller angle corrected for mirrored axes.\n\nFixes #2476\n",
